WEBVTT

00:29:58.350 --> 00:30:00.370
on the ISS.

00:30:00.394 --> 00:30:03.789
AG: Three-hundred and forty
consecutive days in space.

00:30:03.813 --> 00:30:06.116
It's an American record
for a single mission.

00:30:07.017 --> 00:30:10.047
The rest of us weren't schooled
in how to stay at home that long

00:30:10.071 --> 00:30:11.376
in sustained isolation,

00:30:11.400 --> 00:30:14.736
so I turned to Scott for ideas
on building resilience.

00:30:14.760 --> 00:30:18.096
Other than the few fellow space travelers
in isolation with him,

00:30:18.120 --> 00:30:20.597
communication with his family,
friends and coworkers

00:30:20.621 --> 00:30:23.626
was entirely through video,
e-mail and radio calls.

00:30:24.119 --> 00:30:26.556
He couldn't go outside
without the right equipment,

00:30:26.580 --> 00:30:29.746
and he didn't even know when
his mission was going to end.

00:30:29.770 --> 00:30:31.210
Sound familiar?